    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d672">

                <pb facs="0952" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg824"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79620 Boeing Airplane Co./26: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Uruguay</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gade</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-11T21:00:00-03:30"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11, 1928—9
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 12—3:52 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>16. My telegram No. 15, May 11, 10 a.m. O’Neill was unaccompanied on flight, is
                    expected to leave hospital tomorrow.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d672-f1"/> Aeroplane
                    badly damaged.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gade</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d672-f1" n="11" xml:id="d672-f1-content">
                <p>For further activities of Captain O’Neill, see <ref target="#pg825">pp. 825</ref>
                    ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
